X-Build-Environment: This package is designed to be built in a CUDA container
 environment that provides the necessary SDK and Python packages:
 .
 - Ubuntu 22.04 + CUDA 12.8 (nvidia/cuda:12.8.0-devel-ubuntu22.04), the
   FlagOS NVIDIA DEB ABI matrix (FEP-0019)
 - Python 3.12 (deadsnakes) with PyTorch 2.10.0+cu128, Triton 3.6.0 and
   pybind11 3.0.3 via pip (pinned in
   packaging/debian/build-helpers/python-build-requirements.txt)
 - fmt (>= 8.1.1), SQLite3 via system packages; nlohmann-json 3.11.3 (the
   pinned libtriton_jit revision requires >= 3.11.3, Ubuntu 22.04 ships 3.10.5)
   installed from the Ubuntu 24.04 header-only package at image build time
 .
 The Build-Depends listed above are for the Debian packaging tools only.
 CUDA and Python deps are provided by the container environment.

Package: libflagfft-nvidia
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, python3.12
Description: FlagFFT — C++ FFT library for FlagOS (NVIDIA backend)
 FlagFFT is a cuFFT-style FFT library with Triton/TLE code generation,
 targeting FlagOS multi-vendor accelerators. The NVIDIA backend uses
 CUDA + Triton-JIT for kernel generation.
 .
 This package contains libflagfft.so, its private
 libflagfft_triton_jit.so dependency, and the flagfft_codegen Python package
 invoked at plan creation time.
 .
 The JIT code generator requires Python 3.12 (the interpreter libflagfft
 embeds). On Ubuntu 22.04, where the default python3 is 3.10, install
 python3.12 (e.g. from the deadsnakes PPA) and set FLAGFFT_PYTHON=python3.12;
 on Ubuntu 24.04 the default python3 already is 3.12. It does not require the separately packaged
 libtriton-jit runtime.

Package: libflagfft-nvidia-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libflagfft-nvidia (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: FlagFFT development files (NVIDIA backend)
 FlagFFT is a cuFFT-style FFT library with Triton/TLE code generation.
 .
 This package contains the header files for building applications against
 libflagfft-nvidia.
